matology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s110\",\"d3\",4989,5372,\"You have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s111\",\"d3\",5372,5741,\"In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s112\",\"d3\",5741,6073,\"Each one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s113\",\"d3\",6073,6453,\"Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Research Grant’ version of your grant type on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Research Grants.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s114\",\"d3\",6453,6848,\"If you have questions about your eligibility, you can contact us at [email protected] before submitting an application.\\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s97\",\"d3\",0,386,\"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nEHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nEHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nConnect & Network\\nClinical practice\\nEducation & Training\\nResearch & Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s98\",\"d3\",386,762,\"EHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nCongress archive\\nScientific meetings\\nMembership\\nEHA2027 registration\\nEHA2027 program\\nEHA2027 abstract submission\\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\\nEHA2027 sustainability\\nEHA2026 Congress platform\\nEHA2026 sustainability\\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\\nEHA2026 gallery\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s99\",\"d3\",762,1143,\"EHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\\nEHA2025 gallery\\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\\nEHA2024 report\\nEHA2024 gallery\\nEHA2023 report\\nEHA2023 gallery\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\nTrial membership\\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\\nEmeritus membership\\nJoint EHA and national society membership\\nUsing MyEHA\\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nOur guidelines initiative\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s100\",\"d3\",1143,1542,\"Guidelines by areas of disease\\nEHA Guidelines app\\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webi